  "comments": "<p>Varieties are known.<br><br><i>Obverse</i><br>There are two main groups of Obverse.<br>Die <strong>I </strong>- type of font in which \"9\" is open.<br>Die <strong>II</strong> - type of font in which \"9\" is close.<br>Picture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637f644047e02.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637f644047e02.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br><u>1962</u><br>Die <strong>I.1</strong> - \"9\" open, narrow script, the first \"S\" in ČESKOSLOVENSKÁ and \"T\" are in fine lines.<br>Die <strong>I.2</strong> - \"9\" open, wide script, the first \"S\" in ČESKOSLOVENSKÁ and \"T\" are in bold lines.<br>Picture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637f646d8f59a.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637f646d8f59a.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br><u>1963</u><br>Die <strong>I.1</strong> - \"9\" open, narrow script, \"3\" high.<br>Die <strong>I.2</strong> - \"9\" open, wide script, \"3\" low.<br>Picture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637f648bce4ab.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637f648bce4ab.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br><br><i>Reverse</i><br>Reverses of coins N#2017 and N#2645 looks similar, that is why their classification is combined.<br>Die <strong>C</strong> - narrow script, \"1\" with short nose, wide leaf to the left of bottom \"1\", long outer leaves to the right of conjunction.<br><br>Combinations:<br><strong>I</strong>+<strong>C</strong>: 1961, 1962 I.1, 1962 I.2, 1963 I.1, 1963 I.2, 1964, 1965.<br><strong>II</strong>+<strong>C</strong>: 1966-1971.<br>Obverse. <strong>50 heller N# 3273</strong> +Reverse. <strong>C</strong>: 1963.</p>",
